// One issue to one reviewed, test-passing change, run on this Mac.
// Plan, implement, fix and review use different model families; fix loops are capped.
// Plan, implement and fix run vendors' own CLIs over ACP on their subscriptions (acp-agent.sh
// names the agent and model); review and anything else use Command Code models.
digraph Ship {
    graph [
        goal="Implement the goal file passed with --goal-file",
        rankdir=LR,
        max_node_visits=4,
        model_stylesheet="
            *          { model: deepseek-v4.1-flash; provider: commandcode; }
            #plan      { backend: acp; }
            #implement { backend: acp; }
            #fix       { backend: acp; }
            #review    { model: glm-5.3; provider: commandcode; }
        "
    ]

    start [shape=Mdiamond, label="Start"]
    exit  [shape=Msquare, label="Exit"]

    // Markraft is a patched submodule; a fresh clone of HEAD does not have it.
    prepare [label="Prepare", timeout="15m", on_failure="exit", max_retries=1,
             script="sh .fabro/workflows/ship/disk-guard.sh && sh scripts/prepare.sh && sh scripts/check-patch-drift.sh"]

    // Claude Opus 5.5 on the Claude Max plan.
    // A failed plan or implement fails the run instead of quietly handing off to the next step.
    plan [label="Plan", timeout="20m", goal_gate=true, acp.command="sh .fabro/workflows/ship/acp-agent.sh claude claude-opus-5-5", prompt="
Goal:
{{ goal }}

Read README.md, the files the goal names, and their tests. Do not edit source files.
Write a short numbered plan to .factory/plan.md: the files to change, the tests to add,
and how the change keeps current behaviour. Keep scope to exactly what the goal asks."]

    // Composer 2.5 (standard, not fast) on the Cursor plan.
    implement [label="Implement", timeout="30m", goal_gate=true, acp.command="sh .fabro/workflows/ship/acp-agent.sh cursor composer-2.5", prompt="
Goal:
{{ goal }}

Carry out .factory/plan.md. Match the surrounding code's naming, comment density and idiom.
Write Rust to ~/.agents/skills/rust-best-practices/SKILL.md (BeautifulRust); read it first.
Add the tests the plan names. Before you finish, run `bash .fabro/workflows/ship/verify.sh`
and make it pass; it runs the same checks as the Verify stage.
If your shell tool takes a timeout (for example timeout_ms), give every cargo or verify.sh
command 15 minutes; the default can be as short as 10 seconds. Compiler errors come last,
so read the end of the output. Never edit .fabro/, vendor/, patches/ or .github/."]

    verify [label="Verify", shape=parallelogram, timeout="40m",
            script="bash .fabro/workflows/ship/verify.sh"]

    // GPT-6.1 Sol through Codex on the ChatGPT plan.
    fix [label="Fix", timeout="30m", max_visits=3, acp.command="sh .fabro/workflows/ship/acp-agent.sh codex gpt-6.1-sol", prompt="
The checks or the review failed. Run `bash .fabro/workflows/ship/verify.sh`, with a 15-minute
timeout if your shell tool takes one: it names the failing command after FAILED: and prints the end of its output,
where the real errors are. Also read .factory/review.md if it exists. Fix the cause in the source,
then run verify.sh again until it passes.
Write Rust to ~/.agents/skills/rust-best-practices/SKILL.md (BeautifulRust).
Do not weaken, skip or delete tests to make them pass. Never edit .fabro/, vendor/, patches/ or .github/."]

    // Thorough reviews of test-heavy changes have taken about 20 minutes.
    review [label="Review", timeout="40m", max_visits=2, prompt="
Goal:
{{ goal }}

Read ~/.agents/skills/rust-review/SKILL.md (BeautifulRust) and apply its priorities to the Rust in this change.
Review the change on this branch against the goal: run `git diff HEAD~..HEAD` or compare with the
starting commit, read the changed files and tests. Check correctness, scope creep, tests that
actually exercise the change, and that behaviour users see is unchanged unless the goal says otherwise.
Write findings to .factory/review.md.
Also write .factory/visual containing exactly `yes` if the change alters anything drawn in the
app's own interface (layout, colour, interface text, icons, window chrome) or any animation or
motion, otherwise exactly `no`. File names, saved data, logs and behaviour with no on-screen
change are not visual. When unsure, write `yes`: a visual change waits for the owner.
Keep the review proportionate: judge the change against the goal and the code and tests in this
repository. Do not research outside sources or other projects; finish within about 10 minutes.
End your reply with a JSON object: {\"context_updates\": {\"review_ok\": true}} if it is ready to merge,
or {\"context_updates\": {\"review_ok\": false}} if anything must change."]

    start -> prepare -> plan -> implement -> verify
    verify -> review [label="Pass", condition="outcome=succeeded"]
    verify -> fix    [label="Fail"]
    fix -> verify
    review -> exit [label="Ready", condition="context.review_ok=true"]
    review -> fix  [label="Changes"]
}
